# ResourceLimitExceeded errors propagate through try (is_catchable() == false).
# Uses deep recursion to trigger MAX_CONTINUATION_STACK which is uncatchable.
# The try should NOT catch the error — it should propagate to the test runner.
[
  count-down: [fn [let n]
    [if [= n 0]
      "done"
      [count-down [- n 1]]]]

  # try wraps the recursive call, but ResourceLimitExceeded propagates through
  result: [try [fn [] [count-down 9000]]]
]
=== error
continuation stack depth exceeded
